{"page": 0, "segments": [{"index": 0, "text": "Study Guide: Introduction to\nAlgorithms (CLRS, 4th Edition)", "rects": [[62.25, 72.31846618652344, 465.4501037597656, 99.51046752929688], [62.25, 99.50596618652344, 494.2501220703125, 126.69796752929688]], "audio_url": "/static/sessions/fb2e6454/pages/0/audio/seg_0000.wav", "duration": 5.65}, {"index": 1, "text": "Generated 2026-06-01. Subject: Computer Science /\nAlgorithms. Exam format: Mixed (MCQ, Short Answer,\nProblem-Solving, Essay). Coverage: comprehensive. Target\nlength: ~10000 lines.", "rects": [[92.25, 142.77923583984375, 445.050048828125, 156.375244140625], [92.25, 156.37298583984375, 452.2500305175781, 169.968994140625], [92.25, 169.96673583984375, 495.4499206542969, 183.562744140625], [92.25, 183.56048583984375, 243.45008850097656, 197.156494140625]], "audio_url": "/static/sessions/fb2e6454/pages/0/audio/seg_0001.wav", "duration": 16.875}, {"index": 2, "text": "Chapter-by-Chapter Breakdown", "rects": [[62.25, 212.09133911132812, 364.64990234375, 232.48533630371094]], "audio_url": "/static/sessions/fb2e6454/pages/0/audio/seg_0002.wav", "duration": 2.275}, {"index": 3, "text": "Ch. 1 \u2014 The Role of Algorithms in Computing", "rects": [[62.25, 247.42420959472656, 424.476806640625, 263.331298828125]], "audio_url": "/static/sessions/fb2e6454/pages/0/audio/seg_0003.wav", "duration": 3.725}, {"index": 4, "text": "Named Entities (Terms & Definitions)", "rects": [[62.25, 279.2893981933594, 321.45013427734375, 292.8854064941406]], "audio_url": "/static/sessions/fb2e6454/pages/0/audio/seg_0004.wav", "duration": 3.15}, {"index": 5, "text": "Algorithm: Any well-defined computational procedure that\ntakes some value(s) as input and produces some value(s) as\noutput in a finite amount of time; a sequence of\ncomputational steps that transform the input into the output.", "rects": [[92.25, 308.8431396484375, 495.46044921875, 322.43914794921875], [92.25, 322.4368896484375, 509.8498840332031, 336.03289794921875], [92.25, 336.0306396484375, 437.8500671386719, 349.62664794921875], [92.25, 349.6243896484375, 531.4498291015625, 363.22039794921875]], "audio_url": "/static/sessions/fb2e6454/pages/0/audio/seg_0005.wav", "duration": 16.4}, {"index": 6, "text": "Computational problem: A problem whose statement specifies\nthe desired input/output relationship for problem instances,\ntypically of arbitrarily large size. Problem instance: The input (satisfying whatever constraints\nare imposed in the problem statement) needed to compute a\nsolution to the problem.", "rects": [[92.25, 363.2181396484375, 509.8744201660156, 376.81414794921875], [92.25, 376.8119201660156, 524.2498168945312, 390.4079284667969], [92.25, 390.4056701660156, 351.4501647949219, 404.0016784667969], [92.25, 403.9994201660156, 524.2684936523438, 417.5954284667969], [92.25, 417.5931701660156, 502.64990234375, 431.1891784667969], [92.25, 431.1869201660156, 265.05010986328125, 444.7829284667969]], "audio_url": "/static/sessions/fb2e6454/pages/0/audio/seg_0006.wav", "duration": 21.425}, {"index": 7, "text": "Instance: The input to a problem, e.g., the input sequence\n\u21d431, 41, 59, 26, 41, 58\u21d4 is an instance of the sorting\nproblem.", "rects": [[92.25, 444.7806701660156, 509.8592224121094, 458.3766784667969], [92.25, 458.3744201660156, 481.64996337890625, 471.9704284667969], [92.25, 471.9681701660156, 149.8500213623047, 485.5641784667969]], "audio_url": "/static/sessions/fb2e6454/pages/0/audio/seg_0007.wav", "duration": 12.55}, {"index": 8, "text": "Correct algorithm: An algorithm that, for every problem\ninstance provided as input, halts (finishes its computing in\nfinite time) and outputs the correct solution to the problem\ninstance.", "rects": [[92.25, 485.5619201660156, 488.2698059082031, 499.1579284667969], [92.25, 499.1556701660156, 524.2498168945312, 512.7516479492188], [92.25, 512.7494506835938, 524.2498168945312, 526.3453979492188], [92.25, 526.3432006835938, 157.05003356933594, 539.9391479492188]], "audio_url": "/static/sessions/fb2e6454/pages/0/audio/seg_0008.wav", "duration": 13.675}, {"index": 9, "text": "Incorrect algorithm: An algorithm that might not halt at all\non some input instances, or it might halt with an incorrect\nanswer. Sorting problem (formally): Input: A sequence of n numbers\n\u21d4a1, a2, \u2026, an\u21d4. Output: A permutation (reordering) of the\ninput sequence such that a\u20321 \u2264 a\u20322 \u2264 \u2026 \u2264 a\u2032n.", "rects": [[92.25, 539.9369506835938, 524.2720336914062, 553.5328979492188], [92.25, 553.5307006835938, 517.0498657226562, 567.1266479492188], [92.25, 567.1244506835938, 142.6500244140625, 580.7203979492188], [92.25, 580.7182006835938, 509.8802490234375, 594.3141479492188], [92.25, 594.3119506835938, 510.44989013671875, 607.9078979492188], [92.25, 607.9057006835938, 416.2501220703125, 621.5016479492188]], "audio_url": "/static/sessions/fb2e6454/pages/0/audio/seg_0009.wav", "duration": 25.1}, {"index": 10, "text": "Monotonically increasing order: The order of a sorted\nsequence where elements are non-decreasing. Data structure: A way to store and organize data in order to\nfacilitate access and modifications. Satellite data: Data associated with a key (e.g., all fields\nof a record besides the sort key).", "rects": [[92.25, 621.4994506835938, 473.885009765625, 635.0953979492188], [92.25, 635.0932006835938, 401.85015869140625, 648.6891479492188], [92.25, 648.6869506835938, 524.2661743164062, 662.2828979492188], [92.25, 662.2807006835938, 351.4501647949219, 675.8766479492188], [92.25, 675.8744506835938, 524.2661743164062, 689.4703979492188], [92.25, 689.4682006835938, 337.0501708984375, 703.0641479492188]], "audio_url": "/static/sessions/fb2e6454/pages/0/audio/seg_0010.wav", "duration": 21.225}, {"index": 11, "text": "Record: A key plus its associated satellite data. NP-complete: A class of problems for which no efficient\nalgorithm is known; if an efficient algorithm exists for any\none NP-complete problem, then efficient algorithms exist for\nall of them.", "rects": [[92.25, 703.0619506835938, 445.05706787109375, 716.6578979492188], [92.25, 716.6557006835938, 488.2628173828125, 730.2516479492188], [92.25, 730.2494506835938, 524.2498168945312, 743.8453979492188], [92.25, 743.8431396484375, 524.2498168945312, 757.4390869140625], [92.25, 757.4368896484375, 178.65003967285156, 771.0328369140625]], "audio_url": "/static/sessions/fb2e6454/pages/0/audio/seg_0011.wav", "duration": 18.1}, {"index": 12, "text": "\u2022", "rects": [[77.84765625, 308.8431396484375, 85.04765319824219, 322.43914794921875], [77.84765625, 363.2181396484375, 85.04765319824219, 376.81414794921875], [77.84765625, 403.9994201660156, 85.04765319824219, 417.5954284667969], [77.84765625, 444.7806701660156, 85.04765319824219, 458.3766784667969], [77.84765625, 485.5619201660156, 85.04765319824219, 499.1579284667969], [77.84765625, 539.9369506835938, 85.04765319824219, 553.5328979492188], [77.84765625, 580.7182006835938, 85.04765319824219, 594.3141479492188], [77.84765625, 621.4994506835938, 85.04765319824219, 635.0953979492188], [77.84765625, 648.6869506835938, 85.04765319824219, 662.2828979492188], [77.84765625, 675.8744506835938, 85.04765319824219, 689.4703979492188], [77.84765625, 703.0619506835938, 85.04765319824219, 716.6578979492188], [77.84765625, 716.6557006835938, 85.04765319824219, 730.2516479492188]], "audio_url": "/static/sessions/fb2e6454/pages/0/audio/seg_0012.wav", "duration": 0}, {"index": 13, "text": "\u2022", "rects": [[77.84765625, 308.8431396484375, 85.04765319824219, 322.43914794921875], [77.84765625, 363.2181396484375, 85.04765319824219, 376.81414794921875], [77.84765625, 403.9994201660156, 85.04765319824219, 417.5954284667969], [77.84765625, 444.7806701660156, 85.04765319824219, 458.3766784667969], [77.84765625, 485.5619201660156, 85.04765319824219, 499.1579284667969], [77.84765625, 539.9369506835938, 85.04765319824219, 553.5328979492188], [77.84765625, 580.7182006835938, 85.04765319824219, 594.31414794